   260	## Row 3's product-facing contract (council rounds 120 to 123; A1, clamping, withdrawn)
   261	
   262	**The rule.**
   263	
   264	- **On every store with a `days_completed` table**, finished or not, partial rows or not, an explicit upper bound later than the last
   265	  completed day is refused. The same date gets the same answer whenever it is asked.
   266	- An omitted bound gives the last completed day, as today.
   267	- **Steps but no completed day:** refused as the first day.
   268	- **`days_completed` present with no steps and no completed day** (an empty new store): read as today. An omitted bound gives what
   269	  `default_as_of` gives today (none), and an explicit bound passes.
   270	- **A legacy ledger without the tables:** read as today.
   271	- **Ranges:**
   272	  - `changes(since, to)` excludes its start, so a `since` on or after the resolved `to` is refused;
   273	  - `history(from, to)` includes its start, so a `from` after the resolved `to` is refused and `from` equal to `to` passes.
   274	
   275	**The owner, and what the structural check enforces.**
   276	
   277	- **`service.resolve_bound(conn, bound)`** raises `FirstDayNotCompleted` or `BoundNotCompleted(requested, last_completed_day)`, and is
   278	  idempotent: a bound it has already passed passes again. On an empty store (tables, no steps, no completed day) or a legacy ledger,
   279	  an omitted bound resolves to what `default_as_of` gives today, which can be `None`.
   280	- **`service.resolve_range(conn, start, end, start_included)`** resolves `end` through `resolve_bound`, then raises
   281	  `RangeNotOrdered(start, end)` when the start is not before the end (`changes`, start excluded) or is after it (`history`, start
   282	  included).
   283	- `error_response` maps all three exceptions.
   284	- **Every public function that takes a date resolves it at its entry through `resolve_bound`:**
   285	  - `service`: `summaries`, `views`, `view`, `evidence`, `history`, `record`, `changes`, `evaluate`;
   286	  - `bundle`: `not_judged`, `view_bundle`, `days`, `thesis_bundles`, `library`;
   287	  - `idea.read_idea` and `search.search`.
   288	- Nested calls pass a resolved bound, which resolves again unchanged. That covers `view_bundle` called directly with no date (as
   289	  `scripts/mock_data.py` does), or from `_bundles` and `idea.read_idea`.
   290	- **Internal helpers that take a date** (`dependencies`, `dependants`, `evidence_record`, `is_open_as_of`, `state_as_of`, `visible`,
   291	  `_bundles`, …) receive their caller's resolved bound. That is `None` on an empty store, as today, and they behave as today with it.
   292	  Each public function's output on an empty store is the same before and after the change; the test records today's outputs first.
   293	- **A view not visible at the resolved day is refused** (`KeyError`, 404) by `bundle.view_bundle` and `bundle.not_judged` when called
   294	  directly, as `_bundles` already skips it. So a question and its choices created after that day are never returned.
   295	- **The structural check** reads every function of `service`, `bundle`, `search` and `idea` with a date parameter (`as_of`,
   296	  `to_day`). Each must either call `resolve_bound` (or `resolve_range`) or be named in the check's list of internal helpers.
   297	  - A function in neither, or a bound resolved by `or default_as_of(...)`, fails the suite.
   298	  - The check's own mutant (a new public function without the call) must fail it.
   299	
   300	**The response, per channel.**
   301	
   302	| Channel | First day not completed | Bound after the last completed day | Range start not before its end |
   303	|---|---|---|---|
   304	| API | 503 `{"error": "the store's first day has not completed"}` | 409 `{"error": "day not completed", "requested": X, "last_completed_day": Y}` | 409 `{"error": "range start not before its end", "start": S, "end": T}` |
   305	| MCP tools | a tool error whose message carries the same fields | the same | the same |
   306	| Streamed Idea route | the status and body, before any header | the same | — |
   307	
   308	- `error_response` returns `(status, payload)`. The two new exceptions get the payloads above, and every other error keeps
   309	  `{"error": message}`. `_answer` and `_stream_answer` send the payload as given.
   310	- **The streamed route, in one transaction:**
   311	  - it opens its connections, begins the read transaction and resolves the bound and first-day check;
   312	  - **only then** does it send its 200 headers and run the Idea work in the same transaction, which it ends after;
   313	  - a refusal is sent as a normal status and body before any header.
   314	  - The Idea work includes model calls, so this transaction lasts the whole request, up to minutes. That is within row 5's
   315	    one-request rule, and it holds back a checkpoint that long.
   316	
   317	**Callers.**
   318	
   319	- **The page, when its live library read succeeds:** it sends only days from the served dataset (`library.getDay()` to `/ideas`;
   320	  the returned `card.idea.as_of` to `/thesis-bundles`). These are never after the last completed day.
   321	- **The page, when its live library read fails:**
   322	  - it keeps its embedded snapshot silently (as `thesis-ui.md` specifies), and that snapshot's day can be later than the service's
   323	    last completed day;
   324	  - `/ideas` is then refused with 409, and the page shows its existing Idea error naming no day;
   325	  - this is documented here and tested; it is not claimed impossible.
   326	- **MCP clients and direct API users with a later date:**
   327	  - on the running product's store, they would get an error naming 2026-08-28 instead of today's half-processed 2026-08-29 (99
   328	    evidence records, 117 links);
   329	  - on a finished store, they would get an error instead of today's identical answer.
   330	  - This is the behaviour change, recorded for Alex.
   331	- **Not deployed:** no running service is restarted. D439 does not authorize a deploy, and the change reaches the running product
   332	  only on a restart, which is on Alex's page.
   333	
   334	**Proofs added to the plan (2b to 2e):**
   335	
   336	- 2b. The structural check, and its mutant.
   337	- 2c. Each public function called directly with a future bound, an omitted one and a past one, on the four store states (finished,
   338	  partial, first day, empty with tables) and a copy of the served store's state. Each call's actual output or error is compared
   339	  with the expected one: today's recorded output where the rule keeps it, the named refusal where the rule changes it.
   340	- 2c′. `view_bundle` and `not_judged` called directly for a view created after the resolved day are refused (404). `days()` on an
   341	  empty store returns `[]` as today.
   342	- 2d. The ranges: `changes` with `since` equal to its end is refused; `history` with `from` equal to `to` passes.
   343	- 2e. The streamed route on a first-day store and with a future date: a status before any header. With a writer committing during
   344	  an Idea request, the request's data are the state at its start.
   345	- 2f. The page verifier (`poc/ui/verify-*.mjs`): live read successful, then the Idea call succeeds; live read failed with a later
   346	  embedded day, then the Idea error shows and nothing else breaks.
   347	
   348	## Not covered
   349	
   350	- Resuming a stopped live store.
